2026-09-26  (direct)  A re-keyed group's pin stays in Favorites: the Mac's pinning plist kept LMT under iCloud group ids
                 that match no chat row any more, so Blip dropped it while the phone still showed it pinned. imsg now
                 resolves pin ids through chat.db's chat_lookup (iMessageGroupID), the table Messages itself uses.
                 gus and vic both show all 9 pins in the phone's order. Fred Nix / Larry, X https://x.com/nixfred
2026-09-25  #115 Opt-in glide for mouse-wheel notches: smooth_scroll=on in bridge.conf animates a notch 180 ms OutCubic,
                 retargeted (a notch mid-glide moves the target, never restarts the easing), cancelled by any other contentY
                 write; touchpads never animate. The PR shipped it ON by default behind a shell.json setting and rewrote the
                 "never animate wheel scroll" invariant; Fred chose opt-in, default OFF, bridge.conf key: the invariant came from
                 his MX Master, whose one click is four notches, and Guido tested on a plain wheel plus an offscreen harness
                 only. Default flips on Fred's hand, not on a harness. Merged with the change, 632 tests, deployed key-absent.
                 Guido Jouret, github.com/gjouret, X https://x.com/gjouret
2026-09-25  (direct)  scroll_gain= and touchpad_scroll_gain= in bridge.conf (0.05-10, default 1, re-read on save, shown by
                 `status`). One physical click of an MX Master 4 is FOUR notches (raw evdev: bursts of 4,4,4,3 in 0.13 s), so
                 even at Guido's 1:1 one click was 480 px in a 609 px window; gus and vic run 0.25 (~120 px per click).
                 FOUND WHILE VERIFYING: the #113 deploy on 23 Sep left nixfred.blip.bak-113-<ts> inside
                 ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/ on both hosts; PluginRegistry scans plugins/* in glob order and the last manifest
                 id wins, so the pre-#113 backup was what actually ran on gus AND vic until today, through three deploys
                 that reported healthy=true. #113 and #114 are live as of 25 Sep. Backups now go to
                 ~/.local/state/omarchy/plugin-backups/. Fred judged 0.25 by hand the same evening: keeper.
                 Fred Nix / Larry, X https://x.com/nixfred
2026-09-25  #114 One wheel notch scrolls one notch. The conversation and the thread list multiplied every wheel event by 4.5
                 (a standard notch, angleDelta 120, moved about 540 px) and touchpad deltas by 3, on top of the scroll factor
                 Hyprland had already applied, so Blip alone scrolled 4.5x faster than every other app. Both handlers now
                 apply the delta 1:1 through two BlipView properties (wheelMultiplier, touchpadMultiplier, default 1.0). The
                 4.5 dated from the 1.3.4 fix and was never measured against another app. Fred chose 1:1 and judges by hand;
                 a bridge.conf key is the next step if it is too slow. On gus the MX Master 4 goes 540 -> 120 px per notch and
                 the Elan touchpad (scroll_factor 0.4) 1.2 -> 0.4 px per px. Not verified by hand: touchpad feel (he has none).
                 Guido Jouret, github.com/gjouret, X https://x.com/gjouret
2026-09-23  #113 Turning the only monitor off with the Blip window open no longer crashes Hyprland. Qt swaps the lost output
                 for a nameless 0x0 placeholder screen, Omarchy builds a bar on it, and Blip's widget there crowned itself
                 leader and mapped the app window with no output, a null dereference in Hyprland 0.56.2's floating layout.
                 The leader rule now lives in screen-leader.ts and nobody leads while no real screen exists. Verified in
                 Test Drive with an instrumented build: the placeholder is ["",0,0] and got leader=false; the segfault itself
                 was not reproducible there because Hyprland stands up a FALLBACK output in the same event.
                 Brad Larson, github.com/followbl, X https://x.com/followbl
